<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Saurashtra State</h1><p class="st-meta">1948 CE – 1956 CE · capital Rajkot</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The union that merged more than 200 Kathiawar princely states into one Indian state in 1948, with its capital at Rajkot.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> was a patchwork of over two hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar State</a> and Nawanagar to tiny estates. In early 1948, under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/v-p-menon">V. P. Menon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vallabhbhai-patel">Sardar Patel</a>, the rulers agreed to merge their states into the United State of Kathiawar, inaugurated in February 1948; <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/junagadh-state">Junagadh State</a> joined in 1949.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/digvijaysinhji">Jam Sahib of Nawanagar</a>, Digvijaysinhji, served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a>, while an elected government led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-n-dhebar">U. N. Dhebar</a> ran the administration from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajkot-state">Rajkot</a>. Renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, it became a Part B state of the Indian Union in 1950. Its governments carried out land reform that abolished the girasdari and barkhali landholdings of the old nobility.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the States Reorganisation Act <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> was merged into the enlarged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> on 1 November 1956. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> was divided in 1960, the region became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saurashtra-state.jpg" alt="Saurashtra State" width="320" height="387"><figcaption>Image: India 1951 Bombay.svg: Superbenjamin this file: Furfur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saurashtra_in_India_(1951).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1948 CE – 1956 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rajkot</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Digvijaysinhji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Jainism; Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United State of Kathiawar, United State of Saurashtra</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=saurashtra-state" aria-label="Saurashtra State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6576 1354 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Saurashtra State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6896 1610L7018 1386M6896 1610L6936 1629M6896 1610L6909 1585M6896 1610L6892 1638M6896 1610L6875 1604M6896 1610L6868 1634M6896 1610L6898 1622M6896 1610L6894 1592M6896 1610L6898 1599M6896 1610L6884 1601M6896 1610L6928 1638M6896 1610L6896 1610M6896 1610L6912 1606M6896 1610L6921 1601M6896 1610L6895 1631M6896 1610L6896 1641M6896 1610L6908 1620M6896 1610L6915 1631M6896 1610L6930 1626M6896 1610L6914 1602M6896 1610L6920 1604M6896 1610L6913 1598M6896 1610L6920 1590M6896 1610L7110 1534M6896 1610L6917 1578M6896 1610L7356 1591M6896 1610L6962 1578M6896 1610L6883 1639M6896 1610L6885 1652M6896 1610L6972 1626M6896 1610L7014 1623M6896 1610L6901 1618M6896 1610L6920 1662M6896 1610L6893 1634M6896 1610L6897 1613"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1386h0M6936 1629h0M6909 1585h0M6892 1638h0M6875 1604h0M6868 1634h0M6898 1622h0M6894 1592h0M6898 1599h0M6884 1601h0M6928 1638h0M6896 1610h0M6912 1606h0M6921 1601h0M6895 1631h0M6896 1641h0M6908 1620h0M6915 1631h0M6930 1626h0M6914 1602h0M69